<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Järva County</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Järvamaa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Järva County is a county in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, with its centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paide">Paide</a>. The historic land of Järvamaa, called Jerwen in German, came under the Livonian Order in the 13th century, which built a castle at Weissenstein, now Paide. In 1561 its knighthood submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> together with those of Harrien and Wierland, as the Livonian state collapsed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jarva-county.jpg" alt="Järva County" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hannu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tammsaare-P%C3%B5hja_farm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
